1
00:00:01,190 --> 00:00:02,293
Ji?

2
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:04,901
Ji, is that you?

3
00:00:05,454 --> 00:00:08,516
Wow, you’re all grown up.

4
00:00:09,105 --> 00:00:11,970
(You knew Ruth before, Ji?)

5
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,218
How come you never told me that?

6
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:16,676
Why does it say ‘Theeraruth’?

7
00:00:16,945 --> 00:00:18,670
Isn’t his name Atiwitch?

8
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,120
It’s a long story.

9
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:40,000
Ji! Ji!

10
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:41,323
- Ji, baby!
- Ji!

11
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:46,058
- Oh.
- I know the truth.

12
00:00:46,465 --> 00:00:47,309
Aren’t you mad?

13
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,127
You never came to me and said hi.

14
00:00:49,403 --> 00:00:50,945
And I forgot all about us.

15
00:00:50,974 --> 00:00:51,974
Let’s call it even.

16
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:57,120
Now that my parents know we’re friends again,

17
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:00,029
they want you to come over for dinner.

18
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:01,680
Good evening.

19
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:02,821
Good evening.

20
00:01:03,287 --> 00:01:05,280
My mom and dad wanted me to give you this.

21
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:14,981
I’m Kwan from Class 2.

22
00:01:15,163 --> 00:01:17,025
You know Kwan?

23
00:01:17,534 --> 00:01:17,970
Yeah.

24
00:01:18,138 --> 00:01:19,280
The drama club president.

25
00:02:56,029 --> 00:02:57,229
YELLOW TIGER

26
00:02:57,243 --> 00:02:58,836
(PURPLE SCORPION)

27
00:02:58,872 --> 00:03:00,130
(BLUE SHARK)

28
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,458
Sorry. Excuse me.

29
00:03:04,494 --> 00:03:07,083
- Sorry.
- Sorry. Sorry.

30
00:03:13,541 --> 00:03:14,036
There.

31
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:15,494
Okay.

32
00:03:15,694 --> 00:03:17,650
- Need any more help?
- No, that’s all.

33
00:03:18,043 --> 00:03:19,650
You’re free until the parade’s over.

34
00:03:20,632 --> 00:03:21,632
- Let’s go.
- Let’s go.

35
00:03:22,218 --> 00:03:24,436
- Grilled pork.
- Let’s get grilled pork.

36
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:32,021
Would you like a zodiac reading?

37
00:03:33,258 --> 00:03:34,283
Let’s do this one.

38
00:03:34,312 --> 00:03:36,392
Arrange the flower, leaf,

39
00:03:36,429 --> 00:03:38,196
mountain, and sun in your preferred order.

40
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:39,840
(Hmm...)

41
00:03:40,050 --> 00:03:43,512
(The sun, leaf, mountain, flower.)

42
00:03:43,534 --> 00:03:45,861
The sun, leaf, mountain, flower.

43
00:03:46,341 --> 00:03:48,218
Okay, let me read it for you.

44
00:03:48,516 --> 00:03:50,167
Your fortune says...

45
00:03:50,196 --> 00:03:52,690
Your relationship with him is like a lemon.

46
00:03:52,727 --> 00:03:55,214
Sweet and sour, fizzy, and refreshing.

47
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:57,789
Your love life is so enviable right now that

48
00:03:57,818 --> 00:03:59,469
single people would be jealous.

49
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:03,578
But beware of the bitter taste of the lemon peel.

50
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:06,072
That person is keeping a secret from you.

51
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:25,890
NAWINA SCHOOL

52
00:04:25,934 --> 00:04:28,421
Ji, about the lunch boxes…

53
00:04:34,930 --> 00:04:38,109
Oh, my mom said she’ll drop them off
in front of the school.

54
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:41,490
You can pay after the budget has been approved.

55
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,380
Are you okay?

56
00:04:45,018 --> 00:04:46,152
Is there something wrong?

57
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:48,356
Nothing.

58
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,360
We’ve brought the bottled waters since yesterday.

59
00:04:55,985 --> 00:04:57,454
Shouldn’t you be at the competition?

60
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,552
We’re leaving at 7.

61
00:05:00,596 --> 00:05:01,596
I’ll be gone soon.

62
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:05,243
I probably won’t see you again today.

63
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,876
Have fun on the Sports Day.

64
00:05:13,869 --> 00:05:15,860
I’m off now.

65
00:05:16,341 --> 00:05:17,341
Mmm.

66
00:05:17,490 --> 00:05:18,490
Good luck.

67
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:31,220
Jeez!

68
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,040
What are you looking at?

69
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,600
Nothing.

70
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:36,050
“Good luck.”

71
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,792
Here, Ji.

72
00:05:44,843 --> 00:05:45,843
Thank you.

73
00:05:46,014 --> 00:05:47,076
Where’s Ty?

74
00:05:47,374 --> 00:05:49,032
Oh, he has an upset stomach.

75
00:05:49,061 --> 00:05:50,579
He ate too much grilled pork with sticky rice.

76
00:05:50,603 --> 00:05:52,014
- Poor boy.
- Oh.

77
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,654
Being sick on the Sports Day.

78
00:05:55,272 --> 00:05:57,105
I’ll go, then.

79
00:05:57,483 --> 00:05:58,901
Thank you. See you later.

80
00:05:58,938 --> 00:06:00,545
Bye-bye. See you later.

81
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:01,658
Go.

82
00:06:01,890 --> 00:06:02,890
Let’s go, honey.

83
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:06,058
Can’t you sing louder?

84
00:06:06,094 --> 00:06:07,294
Don’t you see the other teams?

85
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,641
We didn’t ask you to come practice during
your school break.

86
00:06:09,665 --> 00:06:11,401
We’ve prepared free food and drinks for you.

87
00:06:11,425 --> 00:06:12,734
We’re not doing any formations.

88
00:06:13,098 --> 00:06:15,018
All you have to do is sit there, sing, and clap.

89
00:06:15,381 --> 00:06:16,821
Why can’t you even do that properly?

90
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:18,880
Next, we’ll practice…

91
00:06:18,916 --> 00:06:20,456
You’ve been practicing since this morning.

92
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,560
Why don’t you take a break?

93
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,360
- But...
- You can take a break and have some water.

94
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,880
The kids might faint during the cheering competition.

95
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,687
Ten-minute break! Don’t leave the stands.

96
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,716
Here are your drinks.

97
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:43,432
Pass them along.

98
00:06:46,109 --> 00:06:47,109
Thank you.

99
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,710
You volunteered to be the cheer squad leader

100
00:06:51,490 --> 00:06:54,450
because you didn't like being yelled at by your seniors in Grade 7, right?

101
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:58,860
Yeah.

102
00:07:00,356 --> 00:07:01,356
You're right.

103
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,120
My parents have just allowed me to
participate in school activities.

104
00:07:07,910 --> 00:07:10,581
I saw how hard the other teams were working,

105
00:07:10,618 --> 00:07:13,549
so I... wanted to beat them.

106
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:15,830
Thank you.

107
00:07:17,010 --> 00:07:18,010
Mmm.

108
00:07:18,196 --> 00:07:19,621
Oww!

109
00:07:19,672 --> 00:07:21,687
- Ji, The Good Boy.
- Stop it.

110
00:07:21,716 --> 00:07:23,585
- Ji, The Good Boy.
- That’s enough.

111
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,000
The school nurse told me to get some rest.

112
00:07:27,170 --> 00:07:28,170
But I’m just so strong.

113
00:07:28,814 --> 00:07:30,614
I felt better as soon as I took the medicine.

114
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:37,258
Hold on, Ji. Here it comes again.

115
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:41,432
Do you need any help?

116
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:43,672
No, thank you. I’m almost done.

117
00:07:43,694 --> 00:07:45,214
- You should help them instead.
- Okay.

118
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,890
I told you I’m good.

119
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,240
You should…

120
00:07:56,730 --> 00:07:58,065
Hello, ma’am.

121
00:07:58,843 --> 00:07:59,890
How are you doing?

122
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:02,020
Aren’t you afraid of me anymore?

123
00:08:02,909 --> 00:08:05,578
Now you're brave because you have
someone backing you up, huh?

124
00:08:07,690 --> 00:08:10,356
Could you tell Ms. Mai

125
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:13,360
that my classmates really liked the extra worksheets?

126
00:08:13,912 --> 00:08:15,432
Could she make some more for us?

127
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,480
Would you like some drinks?

128
00:08:21,090 --> 00:08:22,712
I can’t stand a kid like you.

129
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:24,710
I’m not your biggest fan, either.

130
00:08:35,210 --> 00:08:37,127
Are they having fun down there?

131
00:08:37,149 --> 00:08:39,539
Your favorite student, Jiraphat, asked me to tell you he loved your worksheets.

132
00:08:39,563 --> 00:08:40,563
Are you happy?

133
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:45,883
You should know that wasn’t what he meant.

134
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,432
Perceptive kid like him

135
00:08:49,469 --> 00:08:51,607
must know you're the one who made those worksheets.

136
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:21,840
Say cheese. Okay.

137
00:09:21,876 --> 00:09:23,425
A candid shot.

138
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:25,294
Yeah, yeah. That’s good.

139
00:09:25,323 --> 00:09:26,443
One-finger pose.

140
00:09:29,410 --> 00:09:30,887
That’s a good one.

141
00:09:30,923 --> 00:09:31,418
YELLOW TIGER, BLUE SHARK,

142
00:09:31,447 --> 00:09:32,516
PURPLE SCORPION Hey, Gun.

143
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,840
You did great getting second place.

144
00:09:35,498 --> 00:09:36,523
Hey, hey.

145
00:09:36,550 --> 00:09:38,909
Oww, oww, oww.

146
00:09:38,938 --> 00:09:40,050
I was praising him.

147
00:09:40,072 --> 00:09:41,789
Why are you sitting on me, Ji?

148
00:09:41,818 --> 00:09:42,818
Ji!

149
00:09:43,229 --> 00:09:46,196
- Oww! Oh, god.
- Oh!

150
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,360
Oww, oww, oww!

151
00:09:47,389 --> 00:09:48,567
- Oww, oww!
- Oww! Help!

152
00:09:48,596 --> 00:09:50,116
- Help me!
- Oww!

153
00:09:50,632 --> 00:09:51,723
Oww, oww!

154
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:53,620
What are you guys doing?

155
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,040
Down.

156
00:09:59,309 --> 00:10:00,414
Umm, sir…

157
00:10:00,749 --> 00:10:02,625
Could you take a picture for us?

158
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,476
- Fine.
- With my brand-new phone.

159
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:07,956
Is the camera on?

160
00:10:07,985 --> 00:10:09,490
- 1... 2... 3.
- Say cheese.

161
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,960
Oh, my hands were shaking. One more.

162
00:10:11,105 --> 00:10:12,105
1…

163
00:10:13,030 --> 00:10:14,109
Body shot.

164
00:10:14,407 --> 00:10:15,221
Nice!

165
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:16,327
1…2…

166
00:10:16,370 --> 00:10:17,370
Kissing pose.

167
00:10:18,930 --> 00:10:19,930
Look like a monkey.

168
00:10:20,138 --> 00:10:21,665
- You mean us?
- Just you.

169
00:10:21,694 --> 00:10:22,694
You, too.

170
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:25,294
See? I took that one.

171
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:27,680
You like it?

172
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,912
The foreground is so blurry.

173
00:10:29,934 --> 00:10:31,174
None of the pictures are clear.

174
00:10:31,636 --> 00:10:33,276
You didn't get any good shots of us, sir.

175
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:37,280
It looks like you took these with a calculator, not a phone.

176
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,450
Ouch!

177
00:10:40,487 --> 00:10:42,210
One for each of you.

178
00:10:45,730 --> 00:10:47,370
YELLOW TIGER, BLUE SHARK, PURPLE SCORPION

179
00:10:49,130 --> 00:10:51,490
Who will represent the Blue Team in
the eating race?

180
00:10:51,716 --> 00:10:53,323
Me, me, me.

181
00:11:03,345 --> 00:11:04,345
3…

182
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:05,770
2…

183
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:07,130
1.

184
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:11,580
Swallow it.

185
00:11:12,392 --> 00:11:13,392
Swallow it.

186
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:15,760
Come on, Tyler.

187
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,338
Tyler! Tyler!

188
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,421
Go, go, go, go.

189
00:11:30,465 --> 00:11:32,356
Tyler! Tyler! Tyler! Tyler!

190
00:11:44,312 --> 00:11:46,276
Woo!

191
00:11:46,312 --> 00:11:50,349
(Next up is the three-legged race.)

192
00:11:50,567 --> 00:11:54,065
(Please send your representatives within
15 minutes.)

193
00:11:54,632 --> 00:11:57,767
Who wants to represent us in the three-legged race? Raise your hand.

194
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:01,520
Stop right there, Tyler. The three-legged race
is a team event.

195
00:12:01,861 --> 00:12:03,869
You only have one competition slot left.

196
00:12:03,898 --> 00:12:05,378
You should compete in something else.

197
00:12:05,527 --> 00:12:06,836
Who else, then?

198
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:12,620
I’ll do it.

199
00:12:14,770 --> 00:12:16,865
I’ll go with Ji.

200
00:12:16,894 --> 00:12:18,860
Okay. Jiraphat and Tawan, then.

201
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:23,090
- Break a leg!
- Woo!

202
00:12:25,830 --> 00:12:26,830
Sign here.

203
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,100
Umm...

204
00:12:31,309 --> 00:12:32,580
There are ten minutes left.

205
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,065
You can wait at the starting point.

206
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:35,087
I’ll be there.

207
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:06,520
Is this okay?

208
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:20,280
What’s up, my friend?

209
00:13:23,530 --> 00:13:24,530
Hi...

210
00:13:24,756 --> 00:13:25,756
My friend.

211
00:13:29,590 --> 00:13:30,950
But once we cross the finish line,

212
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,100
we won't be just friends anymore.

213
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,840
Ready?

214
00:13:46,792 --> 00:13:47,792
3…

215
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,160
2…

216
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:54,780
1.

217
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:55,469
Woohoo!

218
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:02,436
Class President, can we talk?

219
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,585
Woo!

220
00:15:15,607 --> 00:15:16,607
Well done.

221
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:18,378
Well done.

222
00:15:18,407 --> 00:15:19,549
Nice job, Ji.

223
00:15:19,621 --> 00:15:21,287
That’s my brother.

224
00:15:21,534 --> 00:15:23,054
Another medal for Blue Team.

225
00:15:23,083 --> 00:15:24,465
We’re getting the big trophy.

226
00:15:24,501 --> 00:15:26,189
I know that’s right.

227
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,020
(But once we cross the finish line, )

228
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,192
we won't be just friends anymore.

229
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:38,989
(We won't be just friends anymore.)

230
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:44,283
Yay!

231
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:51,650
- Yay!
- Yay!

232
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:55,512
Yay!

233
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:08,340
What’s the matter?

234
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:14,140
Nothing.

235
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:25,316
Drama Club?

236
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:28,952
The event is in January.

237
00:16:29,345 --> 00:16:30,745
We’ll start right after Sports Day.

238
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,123
Is that your friend, Tyler?

239
00:16:39,207 --> 00:16:40,207
Yeah.

240
00:16:40,378 --> 00:16:41,378
Why did you ask?

241
00:16:43,470 --> 00:16:44,470
Nothing.

242
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,654
Yay!!

243
00:16:52,698 --> 00:16:54,269
Woo!

244
00:16:54,290 --> 00:16:55,789
Good job, Tyler!

245
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:13,912
We gather here together...

246
00:17:25,050 --> 00:17:27,425
Look, Ji. Doggie weenie sausages.

247
00:17:34,390 --> 00:17:35,752
Crab sticks are ready.

248
00:17:35,781 --> 00:17:37,774
- Get them while they’re hot.
- I’ll be back.

249
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:51,323
The student council room.

250
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,898
I mean the president.

251
00:17:53,927 --> 00:17:55,247
He’s at the student council room.

252
00:17:55,803 --> 00:17:56,803
Ji.

253
00:17:57,670 --> 00:17:58,950
You want some fried crab sticks?

254
00:18:03,790 --> 00:18:05,869
You go. I’ll take it from here.

255
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:22,647
- Oh.
- Tyler, hi.

256
00:18:22,683 --> 00:18:23,912
Hello, Lita.

257
00:18:23,992 --> 00:18:24,992
Where did Ji go?

258
00:18:25,090 --> 00:18:26,654
Oh, he went to the bathroom.

259
00:18:26,698 --> 00:18:27,698
Oh.

260
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:30,538
Can I ask you something?

261
00:18:30,792 --> 00:18:31,287
Of course.

262
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:35,316
Which do you like better, crab sticks or sausages?

263
00:18:35,505 --> 00:18:37,985
It has to be... crab sticks.

264
00:18:38,327 --> 00:18:39,425
They're the best.

265
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,869
Even though I know they're not made from real crab,

266
00:18:42,218 --> 00:18:43,687
I still eat them every day.

267
00:18:53,990 --> 00:18:54,990
Hey.

268
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:58,749
How was the Science competition?

269
00:18:59,578 --> 00:19:00,578
It’s the same.

270
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,552
You mean you won again?

271
00:19:12,730 --> 00:19:14,574
Here, want some?

272
00:19:43,190 --> 00:19:44,190
Tyler.

273
00:19:44,734 --> 00:19:45,734
Oh, hi, Ploy.

274
00:19:46,610 --> 00:19:48,305
This is Kwan.

275
00:19:50,021 --> 00:19:51,581
You haven’t joined any clubs, have you?

276
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:54,981
So...

277
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,821
Will you audition for the lead role in the school play for me?

278
00:20:03,418 --> 00:20:09,700
DRAMA CLUB CASTING LIST, LEAD ROLE
RUTH ATIWITCH GRADE 11/1, TYLER GRADE 11/7

279
00:20:11,890 --> 00:20:14,058
Don’t you have to go on stage?

280
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:18,000
You want to hear me sing?

281
00:20:19,770 --> 00:20:20,770
Can I?

282
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:24,545
Let’s leave that to Tawan.

283
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:36,180
But if you want to hear me sing just for you,

284
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:37,580
you can.

285
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:40,380
I’d love to.

286
00:20:53,080 --> 00:21:00,756
MONDAY, NOVEMBER 8, 2010

287
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:45,083
What I said this afternoon,

288
00:21:45,541 --> 00:21:47,570
you know what it meant, right?

289
00:21:51,090 --> 00:21:52,458
(To me, he is Ruth.)

290
00:21:53,620 --> 00:21:55,192
(The actual Ruth.)

291
00:21:56,010 --> 00:21:58,829
(I don’t even see him as Theeraruth,
my childhood friend.)

292
00:22:00,890 --> 00:22:04,065
(I don’t even think about Ruth Atiwitch,
the superstar.)

293
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:12,523
(If I let this relationship happen today, )

294
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:14,858
(when that day comes…)

295
00:22:22,350 --> 00:22:23,350
Don’t worry.

296
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:25,090
Just trust me.

297
00:22:37,090 --> 00:22:38,916
I won the science project competition.

298
00:22:39,940 --> 00:22:40,940
Where’s my reward?

299
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:48,443
And I… just won a three-legged race, too.

300
00:22:51,980 --> 00:22:53,512
So we’re both winners.

301
00:22:56,020 --> 00:22:57,020
I guess so.

302
00:23:13,723 --> 00:23:15,992
It’s you who came into my life

303
00:23:16,036 --> 00:23:18,720
You light up my new beginning

304
00:23:18,756 --> 00:23:22,923
Because of you, I want to keep going

305
00:23:43,090 --> 00:23:44,090
Hello?

306
00:23:44,690 --> 00:23:45,690
(Wake up.)

307
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:48,160
I’m up.

308
00:23:54,450 --> 00:23:55,450
What’s going on?

309
00:23:55,898 --> 00:23:56,898
Nothing.

310
00:23:57,403 --> 00:23:58,963
Just wanted to give you a wake-up call.

311
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:02,510
Good morning.

312
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:06,360
Good morning.

313
00:24:06,909 --> 00:24:08,869
(You don’t need to have breakfast at home today.)

314
00:24:09,301 --> 00:24:10,960
(I had my housemaid prepare one for you.)

315
00:24:11,905 --> 00:24:12,960
You did that for me?

316
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:14,280
Yeah.

317
00:24:14,341 --> 00:24:15,661
So we can eat breakfast together.

318
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:22,960
Together?

319
00:24:25,410 --> 00:24:26,410
Um..

320
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:27,500
Yeah.

321
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,080
(See you, then.)

322
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,440
See you.

323
00:24:46,690 --> 00:24:49,454
NAWINA SCHOOL

324
00:24:54,770 --> 00:24:55,770
Morning.

325
00:24:57,330 --> 00:24:57,883
Hi.

326
00:24:58,330 --> 00:24:59,330
Hi.

327
00:24:59,890 --> 00:25:02,261
Here. From Ms. Narumon.

328
00:25:02,312 --> 00:25:03,520
Your favorite desserts.

329
00:25:05,390 --> 00:25:06,390
Hey.

330
00:25:06,581 --> 00:25:07,701
Breakfast first.

331
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:12,460
“Breakfast first.”

332
00:25:12,981 --> 00:25:13,981
What is it?

333
00:25:14,494 --> 00:25:15,494
- Nothing.
- Nothing.

334
00:25:32,341 --> 00:25:34,340
Will you have dinner at my house after school?

335
00:25:35,990 --> 00:25:37,430
My mom and Peach wanted you to come.

336
00:25:37,658 --> 00:25:38,658
My dad’s not home.

337
00:25:45,320 --> 00:25:48,552
Who is this product being made for?
TUESDAY, DECEMBER 7, 2010

338
00:25:48,581 --> 00:25:50,065
Okay, everyone. Any questions?

339
00:25:54,458 --> 00:25:56,407
Okay, okay. That’s all for today.

340
00:25:56,538 --> 00:25:58,400
Attention, students.

341
00:25:58,436 --> 00:26:01,003
Thank you.

342
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:01,541
Okay.

343
00:26:02,030 --> 00:26:03,665
- Let’s go, Ji.
- And don’t forget to…

344
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:09,687
Don't forget to review your lessons, guys.

345
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:15,214
SCHOOL CO-OP

346
00:26:15,243 --> 00:26:16,243
I’m back.

347
00:26:16,620 --> 00:26:17,410
Come on. Have a seat.

348
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:18,440
Okay.

349
00:26:19,767 --> 00:26:20,767
Wow.

350
00:26:21,447 --> 00:26:23,163
You need to eat some vegetables.

351
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:26,040
That’s enough.

352
00:26:34,330 --> 00:26:35,330
When did this happen?

353
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:37,229
After or before Sports Day?

354
00:26:42,940 --> 00:26:43,940
Umm…

355
00:26:44,749 --> 00:26:45,890
After Sports Day.

356
00:26:47,420 --> 00:26:48,420
I won.

357
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:54,952
You all owe me a milk crepe with extra
whipped cream.

358
00:26:55,236 --> 00:26:56,236
Yeah, yeah.

359
00:26:59,060 --> 00:27:01,105
Hey, don’t worry.

360
00:27:01,381 --> 00:27:02,530
The others don’t know yet.

361
00:27:02,785 --> 00:27:03,890
We won’t tell.

362
00:27:05,890 --> 00:27:07,743
You said the same thing about Jiraphat,
the good boy.

363
00:27:07,767 --> 00:27:08,767
Come on.

364
00:27:09,003 --> 00:27:10,232
I mean it this time.

365
00:27:10,429 --> 00:27:11,429
Okay?

366
00:27:11,781 --> 00:27:12,781
Promise.

367
00:27:13,672 --> 00:27:14,349
- I promise, too.
- I promise, too.

368
00:27:14,370 --> 00:27:15,505
- Promise.
- Promise.

369
00:27:15,745 --> 00:27:16,905
- I promise, too.
- I promise.

370
00:27:18,820 --> 00:27:20,203
Come on. Make a promise.

371
00:27:20,661 --> 00:27:21,837
- We won’t tell anyone.
- Come on.

372
00:27:21,861 --> 00:27:23,760
-Come on,
-I’m not telling anyone.

373
00:27:23,796 --> 00:27:24,785
Yeah.

374
00:27:24,810 --> 00:27:25,978
Promise!

375
00:27:26,029 --> 00:27:27,120
- Yay!
- Quiet.

376
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:31,192
Now Class 7 has another couple.

377
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:32,756
I'm in Class 7, too.

378
00:27:33,112 --> 00:27:34,349
Why can't I get a boyfriend?

379
00:27:34,370 --> 00:27:35,520
So jealous.

380
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:36,570
Another couple?

381
00:27:36,923 --> 00:27:39,294
Yeah. Gun and Thiti.

382
00:27:41,316 --> 00:27:42,316
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

383
00:27:42,552 --> 00:27:43,552
Come on.

384
00:27:44,790 --> 00:27:46,472
Since middle school.

385
00:27:46,501 --> 00:27:48,705
All you guys care about is egg yolk ice-cream.

386
00:27:48,741 --> 00:27:51,214
Stop eating and pay attention to the others.

387
00:27:51,905 --> 00:27:54,050
- Did you know about this, Kong?
- Of course.

388
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:56,280
How did you know?

389
00:27:59,700 --> 00:28:01,229
Ahem.

390
00:28:01,272 --> 00:28:02,272
Listen.

391
00:28:03,090 --> 00:28:06,734
I’ve known for a while that Gun and Thiti were dating.

392
00:28:07,054 --> 00:28:08,509
Once other people found out,

393
00:28:08,836 --> 00:28:10,770
their classmates started teasing them.

394
00:28:10,792 --> 00:28:11,738
Mmm.

395
00:28:11,767 --> 00:28:15,701
Then word got around to a conservative teacher.

396
00:28:16,560 --> 00:28:19,723
Gun and Thiti were called to the discipline office,

397
00:28:21,330 --> 00:28:22,589
even though this school doesn't even

398
00:28:22,610 --> 00:28:24,341
have a rule against dating.

399
00:28:24,370 --> 00:28:25,498
- Mmm.
- Mmm, that’s true.

400
00:28:28,690 --> 00:28:31,665
Then their parents came to the discipline office

401
00:28:31,694 --> 00:28:33,323
and yelled at that teacher.

402
00:28:33,890 --> 00:28:35,890
In the end, the teacher gave in.

403
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:37,760
- Oh, wow.
- Hey.

404
00:28:37,898 --> 00:28:38,443
See?

405
00:28:38,669 --> 00:28:41,250
How come you didn’t know about this?

406
00:28:41,272 --> 00:28:42,272
Right.

407
00:28:42,690 --> 00:28:43,690
How did you not know?

408
00:28:44,145 --> 00:28:45,869
We need to stop eating egg yolk ice-cream.

409
00:28:48,310 --> 00:28:50,232
And you need to start eating vegetables, too.

410
00:28:50,269 --> 00:28:51,534
Don’t even try.

411
00:28:51,550 --> 00:28:52,981
Why don’t you have any vegetables
on your plate?

412
00:28:53,003 --> 00:28:54,298
I don’t like vegetables.

413
00:28:54,312 --> 00:28:55,461
(Please, Ruth. Don’t even try.)

414
00:28:55,483 --> 00:28:57,460
(You haven’t touched the vegetables
I gave you.)

415
00:28:57,767 --> 00:28:59,440
Both of you, stop being picky.

416
00:28:59,483 --> 00:29:01,309
You’re grownups. Just eat them.

417
00:29:04,830 --> 00:29:07,025
(There’s something I shouldn't forget.)

418
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,454
(The fact that)

419
00:29:10,450 --> 00:29:11,869
(he's just a 17-year-old boy.)

420
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:23,494
What’s the matter?

421
00:29:28,340 --> 00:29:29,340
Ji?

422
00:29:30,770 --> 00:29:33,149
Pim, what’s the penalty for abducting a minor?

423
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:34,340
Huh?

424
00:29:37,890 --> 00:29:39,083
Hey, Pim.

425
00:29:40,380 --> 00:29:41,883
I'm going into town to buy something.

426
00:29:42,443 --> 00:29:43,443
Wanna come with me?

427
00:29:43,505 --> 00:29:44,505
Mm, okay.

428
00:29:45,670 --> 00:29:46,670
What about you guys?

429
00:29:46,800 --> 00:29:50,349
Ji and I have a mission today.

430
00:29:51,540 --> 00:29:52,385
A mission?

431
00:29:52,421 --> 00:29:53,421
What mission?

432
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:56,400
It's a secret.

433
00:29:58,290 --> 00:30:00,087
- Fine.
- Let’s go, Pim.

434
00:30:00,116 --> 00:30:00,821
See you.

435
00:30:00,865 --> 00:30:02,145
- Mm, see you.
- See you.

436
00:30:07,860 --> 00:30:09,180
Ji, I have something to tell you.

437
00:30:11,498 --> 00:30:13,490
I'm going to audition for the lead role.

438
00:30:15,790 --> 00:30:18,960
I'm going to be a shining star in the sky,

439
00:30:18,996 --> 00:30:21,243
a bird soaring freely through the air.

440
00:30:22,967 --> 00:30:23,967
Huh?

441
00:30:25,236 --> 00:30:27,963
CASTING CALL
DRAMA CLUB

442
00:30:28,420 --> 00:30:29,876
Hey Ji, Tyler.

443
00:30:32,270 --> 00:30:33,779
Ji, are you here for the audition, too?

444
00:30:33,803 --> 00:30:35,818
Oh, no. I’m just here to support.

445
00:30:36,050 --> 00:30:37,716
Tyler, do you have a scene partner yet?

446
00:30:38,683 --> 00:30:40,312
If not, want to rehearse together?

447
00:30:40,341 --> 00:30:41,120
So we won't waste any time.

448
00:30:41,360 --> 00:30:42,360
Okay, Ploy.

449
00:30:42,894 --> 00:30:44,036
I'll go get you the scripts.

450
00:30:48,210 --> 00:30:50,072
- Here you are.
- Thanks.

451
00:30:50,305 --> 00:30:51,305
Have a seat.

452
00:30:52,810 --> 00:30:55,301
(Even though I wasn't interested in school activities, )

453
00:30:56,260 --> 00:30:58,269
(I remembered how much people talked)

454
00:30:58,298 --> 00:31:00,378
(about this school play in my previous life.)

455
00:31:00,407 --> 00:31:03,192
They're gonna make it in the entertainment industry for sure.

456
00:31:03,221 --> 00:31:05,272
It's not easy for just anyone to become an actor.

457
00:31:05,309 --> 00:31:08,276
But if you're as handsome and talented
as President Ruth,

458
00:31:08,305 --> 00:31:09,305
then it's possible.

459
00:31:09,454 --> 00:31:10,130
That's true.

460
00:31:10,283 --> 00:31:13,389
This year's Drama Club lead actor has been getting a lot of attention.

461
00:31:13,738 --> 00:31:16,087
How about we sit near the front?

462
00:31:16,123 --> 00:31:18,203
That way, we can take pictures of President Ruth.

463
00:31:27,020 --> 00:31:29,020
Do you want to go inside the air-conditioned room?

464
00:31:29,840 --> 00:31:31,120
You're waiting for Tyler, right?

465
00:31:31,323 --> 00:31:32,472
You can wait inside.

466
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:34,327
It's hot and noisy out here.

467
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:36,320
But I'm not in the club.

468
00:31:36,910 --> 00:31:37,898
It's fine.

469
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:39,621
I'm not asking you to be a judge.

470
00:31:40,380 --> 00:31:41,700
Just go in there and take a seat.

471
00:31:47,352 --> 00:31:49,350
The first audition starts in 10 minutes.

472
00:31:49,650 --> 00:31:50,650
So?

473
00:32:16,830 --> 00:32:17,396
Hey.

474
00:32:17,425 --> 00:32:18,930
Close that damn door already.

475
00:32:18,960 --> 00:32:20,280
The air conditioning is escaping.

476
00:32:27,770 --> 00:32:28,770
Um…

477
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:31,080
This is Thiti.

478
00:32:31,134 --> 00:32:33,174
He writes the script for our school play
every year.

479
00:32:34,390 --> 00:32:35,390
What?

480
00:32:35,614 --> 00:32:38,145
Do you think I just spend all my time
at school and cram school

481
00:32:38,167 --> 00:32:39,727
and don't know how to do anything else?

482
00:32:42,429 --> 00:32:44,540
Hey, hey, hey. Do you think Thiti isn't qualified?

483
00:32:44,581 --> 00:32:45,665
No, no, no.

484
00:32:45,694 --> 00:32:47,425
- He’s perfect for this.
- Perfect.

485
00:32:47,570 --> 00:32:48,705
- So amazing.
- Amazing.

486
00:32:48,741 --> 00:32:49,854
Truly amazing.

487
00:32:50,203 --> 00:32:53,025
And this is Gun, the head of the set design team.

488
00:32:53,556 --> 00:32:55,330
You already know each other, right?

489
00:32:55,883 --> 00:32:57,330
You're both in Class 7.

490
00:32:57,740 --> 00:32:59,100
Everyone, this is Ji from Class 7.

491
00:32:59,469 --> 00:33:01,658
- He's here to help us out today.
- Huh?

492
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:02,821
We haven't decided on his role yet,

493
00:33:02,843 --> 00:33:04,538
but Lita recommended him.

494
00:33:04,560 --> 00:33:06,530
She said he's really good at coordinating things.

495
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:07,454
Right, Ji?

496
00:33:07,767 --> 00:33:08,767
No.

497
00:33:34,174 --> 00:33:35,174
Fah.

498
00:33:35,629 --> 00:33:36,629
Romeo.

499
00:33:37,280 --> 00:33:38,938
Why art thou called Romeo?

500
00:33:56,930 --> 00:33:57,930
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

501
00:34:03,490 --> 00:34:04,490
Ji!

502
00:34:10,660 --> 00:34:12,065
Hello.

503
00:34:49,861 --> 00:34:51,860
Thanks so much, everyone. That's all for today.

504
00:34:52,490 --> 00:34:55,898
Those of you staying for the rest of the auditions, take a 30-minute break.

505
00:34:55,912 --> 00:34:57,505
Grab something to eat, then come back.

506
00:34:57,534 --> 00:34:59,032
Thanks again for today.

507
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:12,680
Ji, aren't you going home?

508
00:35:12,952 --> 00:35:14,152
Tyler will be waiting for you.

509
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:17,127
Is this the only round of auditions?

510
00:35:17,447 --> 00:35:18,487
Will there be another one?

511
00:35:18,632 --> 00:35:19,632
No, this is it.

512
00:35:19,883 --> 00:35:20,883
Why do you ask?

513
00:35:21,910 --> 00:35:24,167
Isn't Ruth auditioning?

514
00:35:24,407 --> 00:35:25,883
Oh, Ruth.

515
00:35:26,980 --> 00:35:28,189
Don't mention that name again.

516
00:35:28,203 --> 00:35:29,265
I'm still bitter about it.

517
00:35:30,620 --> 00:35:31,620
Why?

518
00:35:31,658 --> 00:35:33,512
We'd talked about wanting

519
00:35:33,549 --> 00:35:35,736
our famous student council president
to play the lead role.

520
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:37,178
But he had to withdraw

521
00:35:37,207 --> 00:35:38,727
because he had student council duties.

522
00:35:39,876 --> 00:35:41,870
Then he recommended Tyler instead,

523
00:35:42,043 --> 00:35:44,872
in exchange for... getting us a meeting room
to use.

524
00:35:48,090 --> 00:35:49,643
(What I feared most, )

525
00:35:50,341 --> 00:35:53,250
(Besides a relationship that should
never happen, )

526
00:35:54,240 --> 00:35:57,687
(was that I might unknowingly ruin
his bright future.)

527
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:04,950
Have you been waiting long?

528
00:36:05,620 --> 00:36:06,620
I haven’t.

529
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:09,447
Shall we go, then?

530
00:36:10,080 --> 00:36:13,258
My mom just called and said she'd prepared dinner for us.

531
00:36:50,180 --> 00:36:51,180
Ruth.

532
00:36:56,540 --> 00:36:58,189
I think we should break up.

533
00:37:04,370 --> 00:37:05,370
I’m sorry.

534
00:37:09,850 --> 00:37:10,850
It’s not because of you.

535
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:13,665
About the school play,

536
00:37:14,600 --> 00:37:15,600
it was my own decision.

537
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:18,727
Are you sure?

538
00:37:19,069 --> 00:37:20,952
I heard talent scouts will be there.

539
00:37:21,847 --> 00:37:24,952
You could become a nationally famous
actor someday,

540
00:37:24,989 --> 00:37:26,472
with lots of money.

541
00:37:26,523 --> 00:37:29,243
- To be loved and admired by everyone.
- That's not the life I want.

542
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:30,327
How do you know?

543
00:37:30,647 --> 00:37:33,134
That's the ultimate dream for a lot of people.

544
00:37:33,163 --> 00:37:34,163
I know.

545
00:37:35,990 --> 00:37:36,990
I do.

546
00:37:43,730 --> 00:37:45,440
Because I have lived that life.

547
00:37:49,720 --> 00:37:50,720
What do you mean?

548
00:38:03,810 --> 00:38:05,054
Think about it.

549
00:38:07,530 --> 00:38:08,800
When did I start changing?

550
00:38:18,310 --> 00:38:19,310
Ji?

551
00:38:20,380 --> 00:38:21,380
Jiraphat?

552
00:38:21,607 --> 00:38:23,578
Why are you staring at me like that?

553
00:38:24,218 --> 00:38:26,414
Ms. Suda has been reported.

554
00:38:26,436 --> 00:38:27,621
Did it reach the principal?

555
00:38:27,650 --> 00:38:29,570
The complaint itself isn't the issue.

556
00:38:29,607 --> 00:38:32,407
The issue is who's behind it.

557
00:38:32,436 --> 00:38:35,436
- (Let's cross the overbridge.)
- (We might not get another chance tomorrow.)

558
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:37,592
The photo booth is what came back, not us.

559
00:38:54,065 --> 00:38:55,065
Since when?

560
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:01,061
Not long after you did.

561
00:39:20,460 --> 00:39:21,505
Are you exhausted?

562
00:40:35,710 --> 00:40:38,610
(What do you think brought us here?)

563
00:40:39,745 --> 00:40:41,740
Romeo, do you love me?

564
00:40:42,312 --> 00:40:43,520
I swear by the moon.

565
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:44,760
(Don't be afraid.)

566
00:40:45,229 --> 00:40:46,229
(From now on, )

567
00:40:46,712 --> 00:40:47,752
(wherever you go, )

568
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:49,480
(I'll go with you.)

569
00:40:50,167 --> 00:40:51,410
Mr. President.

570
00:40:52,050 --> 00:40:53,530
What are you doing in the Drama Club?

571
00:40:55,745 --> 00:40:56,749
Why can’t I be here?

572
00:40:56,981 --> 00:40:58,669
(I want to do what we did on Sports Day.)
